WEBVTT

00:26.735 --> 00:28.236
Thank you very much.

00:28.319 --> 00:30.280
I got some good practice in,
thanks to you.

00:30.363 --> 00:31.322
N-No problem.

00:32.032 --> 00:33.074
No way!

00:33.158 --> 00:34.909
Is he really a middle schooler?

00:34.993 --> 00:37.203
Even a college player wouldn't be able
to cleanly catch that pitch!

00:37.287 --> 00:39.914
He's beyond high school level.

00:39.998 --> 00:43.752
I laughed when I first heard about him,
but once you actually see that...

00:44.335 --> 00:46.504
He doesn't even feel human!

00:47.046 --> 00:49.507
No wonder they call him a "Unicorn."

02:20.014 --> 02:23.935
SATURDAY, MAY 9TH

02:24.519 --> 02:27.188
Okay, midterms are next week.

02:27.772 --> 02:28.857
- You serious?
- What a pain!

02:28.940 --> 02:31.693
Starting today, all club activities
are suspended for one week.

02:32.277 --> 02:35.280
Make sure to go over everything
you've covered so far.

02:36.197 --> 02:37.991
So, it's here at last!

02:38.074 --> 02:42.120
Since it's our first test after starting
middle school, I'm kinda nervous!

02:42.704 --> 02:44.038
What about you, Ogami?

02:44.122 --> 02:45.415
Whoa, scary!

02:45.498 --> 02:46.332
Huh?

02:46.416 --> 02:47.959
You look kinda pissed!

02:48.042 --> 02:50.003
No, it's not like that.

02:50.587 --> 02:53.673
More like, "A test!
All right, I'm gonna kill it!"

02:53.756 --> 02:55.425
I mean, the bloodlust is intense!

02:55.508 --> 02:57.218
He straight up looks like an assassin!

02:57.302 --> 03:01.097
Boss, don't go blowing your cover
over something this stupid!

03:02.307 --> 03:05.268
Uh, this is my first time
dealing with midterms!

03:05.351 --> 03:07.020
What should I do, Master?

03:07.103 --> 03:09.022
I mean, it's everyone's first time.

03:09.105 --> 03:11.608
Let's do our best, Noren!

03:11.691 --> 03:12.859
You just suddenly popped up!

03:13.443 --> 03:16.404
Ogami, you're already really good
at studying ahead and reviewing

03:16.487 --> 03:18.823
so I think you'll be fine
just doing what you normally do.

03:19.532 --> 03:22.619
Thank you for your words
of wisdom, Master!

03:22.702 --> 03:24.996
Seriously, what is with that energy?

03:26.706 --> 03:27.624
Morning!

03:27.707 --> 03:28.875
Oh, hey, Noren!

03:28.958 --> 03:29.792
Morning!

03:31.002 --> 03:32.253
So bright!

03:32.337 --> 03:34.464
You're glowing? What happened to you?

03:34.547 --> 03:36.049
So, here's the thing.

03:36.132 --> 03:39.177
During test week, everybody
goes into study mode, right?

03:39.260 --> 03:41.804
Like, nobody's got time
to get all worked up.

03:41.888 --> 03:45.099
Which means nobody's
been confessing their love to me!

03:45.183 --> 03:46.267
R-Right.

03:46.351 --> 03:49.270
I've been sleeping so well
with zero stress!

03:49.354 --> 03:51.689
I wish it could be test week forever!

03:51.773 --> 03:53.900
Man, you've got it rough, too, huh?

03:53.983 --> 03:55.568
I'm actually starting to worry about you.

03:56.152 --> 03:57.070
Oh, sorry.

03:57.654 --> 03:58.571
Huh?

04:00.031 --> 04:02.200
Your face is wrecked!
You're all dried out!

04:02.283 --> 04:03.493
Oh! Morning!

04:03.576 --> 04:05.995
What's with those eye bags?
Did you not sleep?

04:06.079 --> 04:08.331
Huh? What happened to you, Ogami?

04:08.414 --> 04:10.250
"Glowing" and "dried out"?

04:10.333 --> 04:12.669
What is with this couple?
The contrast is insane!

04:13.253 --> 04:15.296
Whoa! Those eye bags are bad!

04:15.380 --> 04:18.216
You really need to get some sleep, Ogami!

04:18.299 --> 04:19.217
Yeah.

04:19.300 --> 04:20.969
I know that logically, but...

04:24.222 --> 04:25.640
Huh? It's morning already?

04:26.224 --> 04:28.726
It's like I just can't stop myself.

04:28.810 --> 04:30.520
How do I put this feeling?

04:32.689 --> 04:35.942
It's kind of like how a boxer knows
rest is important before a match

04:36.025 --> 04:39.279
but still winds up overtraining anyway.

04:39.362 --> 04:41.155
I have no idea what kind
of metaphor that was,

04:41.239 --> 04:43.741
but basically,
you're just trying way too hard?

04:51.249 --> 04:52.458
Want one?

04:52.542 --> 04:53.710
It helps you relax.

04:53.793 --> 04:54.794
I don't need that!

04:56.045 --> 04:57.964
I'm telling you...

04:58.047 --> 04:59.882
you're overdoing it, Boss.

04:59.966 --> 05:02.051
Pipe down. Mind your own business.

05:02.552 --> 05:04.595
Believe me, I'd love to!

05:04.679 --> 05:07.390
Trying to stop someone from studying
too hard is such a ridiculous problem!

05:08.850 --> 05:12.645
I've got other plans tonight,
so go eat dinner at Mama's place, okay?

05:12.729 --> 05:15.189
Huh? I can eat wherever I--

05:15.273 --> 05:16.357
Just go, all right?

05:16.441 --> 05:18.526
Consider it a change of pace.

05:18.609 --> 05:19.610
RAMEN

05:19.694 --> 05:20.903
You can head out now.

05:20.987 --> 05:22.613
Huh? Already?

05:22.697 --> 05:24.824
It's test week, isn't it?

05:24.907 --> 05:26.200
I'm fine.

05:26.284 --> 05:29.412
I may not look it, but I actually
do study seriously on a regular basis.

05:29.495 --> 05:30.663
Doesn't matter.

05:30.747 --> 05:33.958
At this rate, we're not gonna get
many more customers tonight anyway.

05:34.042 --> 05:35.043
Okay.

05:35.626 --> 05:38.046
Then I'm heading out!

05:41.591 --> 05:42.800
Ogami?

05:48.431 --> 05:50.183
Where's he going?

05:52.393 --> 05:54.228
Wait, whoa!

05:54.312 --> 05:56.898
He's heading deeper and deeper
into a really sketchy area!

05:57.398 --> 05:59.734
Oh, Juzo!

06:00.318 --> 06:01.611
Good evening!

06:02.195 --> 06:04.739
Hey. Gekota, was it?

06:04.822 --> 06:06.824
Long time no see, little fish!

06:07.784 --> 06:08.701
You open?

06:08.785 --> 06:12.330
Open for freakin' business, babe!

06:12.413 --> 06:15.249
I came by to score some dinner

06:15.833 --> 06:18.711
but is Kyosuke, I mean Mama, here?

06:18.795 --> 06:20.171
Abso-freakin'-lutely!

06:20.254 --> 06:21.881
Mama Nagisa!

06:21.964 --> 06:25.259
Your itty-bitty boyfriend's here!

06:26.469 --> 06:28.930
W-What kind of setup is this?

06:30.890 --> 06:34.185
No matter how many times I see you,
you're still just too adorable!

06:34.268 --> 06:35.311
I could eat you right up!

06:35.394 --> 06:38.397
Your pilaf's always good, Mama.

06:39.232 --> 06:41.859
My, my... Geko, could I get
an oolong tea for him?

06:41.943 --> 06:43.152
Coming right up!

06:45.696 --> 06:46.531
You know,

06:46.614 --> 06:49.492
if people found out, they'd start
gossiping that I had a secret child,

06:49.575 --> 06:51.619
so I told everyone you're my nephew.

06:51.702 --> 06:52.578
I see.

06:52.662 --> 06:56.499
Honestly, when you first de-aged,
I was stunned.

06:57.959 --> 07:00.211
Oh, Neko, welcome!

07:00.795 --> 07:04.298
Oh my, what's this?
Who's this delicious-looking little cutie?

07:06.801 --> 07:08.386
He's actually Boss.

07:08.469 --> 07:09.428
Huh?

07:10.012 --> 07:14.183
I know I can trust you, and when things
go sideways, you always come through.

07:14.267 --> 07:15.226
So, this really helps.

07:15.309 --> 07:17.895
Leave it to me, little Juzo.

07:17.979 --> 07:20.940
Honestly, now I wanna protect you
even more than before.

07:21.023 --> 07:22.483
I'm beat!

07:22.567 --> 07:24.610
Mama, listen to this.

07:24.694 --> 07:26.904
The new guy screwed up royally today.

07:26.988 --> 07:28.197
Eri?

07:28.281 --> 07:29.574
What are you doing here?

07:29.657 --> 07:31.284
Eri, welcome back!

07:31.367 --> 07:32.618
The usual for you?

07:32.702 --> 07:34.078
Yeah, please!

07:34.162 --> 07:36.831
I tell you, kids these days...

07:36.914 --> 07:38.249
- Oh, stop!
- Kotatsu!

07:38.332 --> 07:40.585
- That's such an old-lady move.
- Jeez, what a pain.

07:43.379 --> 07:45.423
I was wondering how you got
those bags under your eyes.

07:45.506 --> 07:46.507
So, that's what's going on?

07:46.591 --> 07:47.884
Oh, shut up.

07:47.967 --> 07:50.178
Never mind that. Is it okay
for you to be drinking here?

07:50.261 --> 07:51.220
What about Kozue?

07:51.304 --> 07:53.181
It's fine, it's fine!

07:55.141 --> 07:57.518
She lets me get away with stopping in
for one drink every once in a while

07:57.602 --> 07:58.728
while on the way home.

07:58.811 --> 08:01.189
That girl's got a good head
on her shoulders.

08:04.025 --> 08:05.193
I see.

08:05.276 --> 08:06.444
Yeah, I guess she does.

08:10.031 --> 08:11.699
Pulling all-nighters to study...

08:11.782 --> 08:15.870
Why not just go into that test
as you are and bomb it as you are?

08:15.953 --> 08:16.829
Hey, come on!

08:16.913 --> 08:20.249
I'm not asking you to comfort me
or anything, but that's brutal!

08:20.333 --> 08:22.418
No, that's not what I meant.

08:22.502 --> 08:23.336
Huh?

08:25.880 --> 08:27.715
Before you ended up in that body,

08:27.798 --> 08:30.843
when you were still out there working,
the mission was everything.

08:30.927 --> 08:33.054
You were never allowed to fail, right?

08:34.680 --> 08:39.227
Even back when you used to drink here,
part of you was always wound tight.

08:39.936 --> 08:43.356
But I don't think you need
that kind of mindset for studying.

08:43.439 --> 08:46.609
Now that you're a middle schooler,
it's okay to screw up sometimes.

08:47.109 --> 08:49.946
Might as well take advantage of it
and make all the mistakes

08:50.029 --> 08:52.907
you never got to make before,
not just with studying, either.

08:54.242 --> 08:56.911
Besides, setting aside
the sleep deprivation for the moment

08:57.495 --> 08:59.789
ever since you started middle school

08:59.872 --> 09:02.124
you've been looking
a whole lot more alive.

09:05.378 --> 09:06.546
See ya, Mama.

09:06.629 --> 09:08.130
Thanks for the drink!

09:08.214 --> 09:09.966
Okay, see you next time!

09:10.049 --> 09:13.511
And you, quit standing there spacing out
and walk her to the station!

09:13.594 --> 09:14.971
R-Right.

09:18.474 --> 09:20.184
What?!

09:20.268 --> 09:24.855
He went into that crossdresser bar
and came back out with a hot older lady!

09:24.939 --> 09:27.400
Just who is Ogami?

09:27.483 --> 09:28.776
MIDTERM EXAMS (DAY ONE)

09:28.859 --> 09:32.738
In the end, I wouldn't say
I bombed the test

09:32.822 --> 09:36.409
but I made a few careless mistakes,
forgot a few things and did about average.

09:37.118 --> 09:38.578
Well, for this time...

09:39.161 --> 09:40.871
I guess this is about
what I should've expected.

09:40.955 --> 09:43.916
I'll learn from it
and do better on finals.

09:53.843 --> 09:54.885
Come to think of it...

09:54.969 --> 09:57.888
Well, I'm just here for the ramen, so...

09:57.972 --> 10:01.309
Ogami really isn't normal?

10:01.892 --> 10:03.811
So, keep your hands off my girl.

10:03.894 --> 10:05.646
- It's more than just him being weird.
- Now get lost.

10:05.730 --> 10:06.522
What is it?

10:07.481 --> 10:09.609
He feels more like
somebody's uncle or a dad

10:09.692 --> 10:11.944
like he's from
a totally different age group.

10:12.612 --> 10:15.323
Is he really a middle school student?

10:20.036 --> 10:20.953
HOME EC ROOM

10:21.037 --> 10:22.204
Like this...

10:22.788 --> 10:27.543
pass the thread between the button
and the fabric three or four times.

10:28.127 --> 10:32.006
Don't forget to stick your thumb
in here to leave a little slack.

10:32.089 --> 10:34.967
Then wrap the thread
around that slack over and over,

10:35.051 --> 10:36.719
and that gives you the thread shank.

10:36.802 --> 10:38.638
Make a loop.

10:38.721 --> 10:41.390
Pull tight.
And to finish it off, tie a knot.

10:42.933 --> 10:44.685
And there, done.

10:45.269 --> 10:46.979
See? Easy, right?

10:47.063 --> 10:49.774
Oh! So, that's how you sew on a button!

10:49.857 --> 10:52.151
Once you get used to it,
it doesn't even take ten minutes.

10:52.234 --> 10:54.945
And honestly, even just repairing
a button yourself

10:55.029 --> 10:57.365
might make you feel
more attached to your clothes.

10:57.448 --> 10:58.366
I see!

10:58.449 --> 10:59.992
It's like cars and motorcycles.

11:00.076 --> 11:02.495
The more you work on them yourself,
the more attached you get.

11:02.578 --> 11:05.873
That is a weirdly un-middle-schooler-like
way to relate to what I just said.

11:06.457 --> 11:08.125
Anyway, why don't you give it a try?

11:08.709 --> 11:10.586
If there's anything
you don't get, just ask.

11:10.670 --> 11:11.879
'Kay!

11:11.962 --> 11:13.714
So, that's what needles can be used for!

11:13.798 --> 11:14.548
Huh?

11:15.132 --> 11:18.803
I always thought you used them
to coat with poison and stab people.

11:18.886 --> 11:21.055
That's... not wrong, but...

11:23.307 --> 11:24.809
Huh?

11:24.892 --> 11:27.144
The club president made it look easy.

11:28.062 --> 11:29.021
What is that?

11:29.105 --> 11:31.190
- How did you mess it up like that?
- Noren?

11:32.108 --> 11:33.317
Me, too!

11:33.401 --> 11:34.318
Hey...

11:34.402 --> 11:37.905
Doing this again made me realize
I'm actually terrible at sewing!

11:37.988 --> 11:40.616
Well, that's what
club activities are for, right?

11:40.699 --> 11:42.576
I'm gonna go ask the seniors for help!

11:42.660 --> 11:43.828
Me, too!

11:57.174 --> 11:58.050
That's...

11:58.134 --> 11:59.510
Kito!

11:59.593 --> 12:01.053
You're not heading home yet?

12:01.137 --> 12:03.431
Oh, hey, you two!

12:04.014 --> 12:06.350
I forgot to water these guys.

12:06.934 --> 12:08.477
Sunflowers?

12:08.561 --> 12:10.563
Yep. I planted the seeds early

12:10.646 --> 12:13.399
so they should probably bloom
before summer vacation.

12:14.608 --> 12:15.818
I can't wait!

12:18.362 --> 12:20.030
Something happen?

12:20.114 --> 12:21.240
Hmm?

12:21.323 --> 12:24.201
I mean, you seem
like you're in a good mood.

12:25.995 --> 12:27.788
It's not so much that something happened.

12:27.872 --> 12:29.957
It's more like I really like
the Home Ec Club.

12:30.040 --> 12:30.791
Yeah.

12:31.375 --> 12:33.669
Kito loves plants.

12:34.295 --> 12:37.006
President Shiraishi's
into cooking in general.

12:37.089 --> 12:39.008
Yamaoka likes baking sweets.

12:39.633 --> 12:43.095
And Tamada and Nishimura
are really good at handicrafts!

12:43.762 --> 12:46.223
We all do different things
together as a club,

12:46.307 --> 12:50.060
but every one of them has their own
little world that they genuinely love!

12:50.644 --> 12:53.355
So, nobody's just hanging
around to gossip or pry,

12:53.439 --> 12:54.982
and they're all really easy to talk to!

12:55.566 --> 12:58.194
I'm really glad I joined the Home Ec Club!

13:00.905 --> 13:02.907
Um, today's club activity is

13:02.990 --> 13:05.409
making rice balls
to deliver to the baseball team.

13:06.494 --> 13:07.870
It's a lot, so it'll be tough

13:07.953 --> 13:10.956
but they'll really appreciate it,
so let's do our best!

13:11.540 --> 13:13.209
Is something wrong?

13:13.292 --> 13:14.960
Well, the thing is...

13:15.711 --> 13:18.297
our field doesn't just get used
by the middle school baseball team.

13:18.380 --> 13:20.633
We also lend it out
to a Little Senior League team.

13:21.217 --> 13:26.096
Today's delivery is actually for them
and a Unicorn is there.

13:27.681 --> 13:30.518
Yeah, that's the problem.

13:31.101 --> 13:34.980
Just because he's a Unicorn doesn't
automatically mean he's after you, Noren.

13:35.064 --> 13:39.235
That's just a rumor after all,
and it's possible nothing'll happen.

13:39.818 --> 13:41.946
Still, if you two
aren't comfortable with it,

13:42.029 --> 13:44.240
I think it'd be fine
for you not to join in.

13:44.823 --> 13:45.950
It's up to you.

13:47.493 --> 13:48.911
I get how you feel.

13:49.495 --> 13:51.372
So, whatever you decide.

13:54.458 --> 13:56.168
- Move up, move up front!
- One more!

13:56.252 --> 13:57.628
- Let me hear you!
- Ready!

13:58.295 --> 14:00.548
Hey, we brought some snacks for you guys!

14:00.631 --> 14:02.591
Oh, thanks!

14:02.675 --> 14:03.717
Everybody, gather up!

14:04.510 --> 14:06.178
- Thanks!
- No problem!

14:07.263 --> 14:08.347
Looks great!

14:08.430 --> 14:09.348
Time to eat!

14:09.431 --> 14:10.391
Hey, hurry up!

14:11.517 --> 14:12.977
Oh, they're here?

14:13.060 --> 14:14.728
Oh, there.

14:14.812 --> 14:16.605
That tall guy is the one
they were talking about.

14:19.650 --> 14:21.193
I see.

14:21.277 --> 14:24.113
You can tell right away
from the atmosphere.

14:28.492 --> 14:29.910
Tenma Tendo.

14:29.994 --> 14:31.287
He's huge!

14:31.370 --> 14:34.665
Is that really a middle schooler?
He's gotta be pushing 190 cm!

14:34.748 --> 14:36.250
Oh, rice balls!

14:36.333 --> 14:37.501
Thanks a ton!

14:37.585 --> 14:39.169
Sorry I was late getting over here!

14:39.253 --> 14:40.629
Down the hatch!

14:43.465 --> 14:46.176
Man, that's good! Total energy boost!

14:48.095 --> 14:49.680
Oh, right.

14:49.763 --> 14:52.683
You two are here, huh?
Then I wanted to talk to you for a sec!

14:53.267 --> 14:55.394
You're Noren and Juzo, right?

14:55.477 --> 14:57.313
You've been getting
a lot of attention lately.

14:57.980 --> 14:59.189
He's a giant!

14:59.773 --> 15:02.818
All right then, let's see
whether the rumors are true.

15:03.360 --> 15:05.988
Either way, I figure he won't come
right out with it immediately, but...

15:06.071 --> 15:07.406
Let's duel.

15:08.157 --> 15:11.410
If I win, I get to be
Noren's boyfriend, right?

15:11.493 --> 15:12.870
Wha...

15:12.953 --> 15:16.040
Oh, come on. So, the rumors are true
and you're opening with that?

15:16.123 --> 15:17.791
Oh no!

15:17.875 --> 15:19.376
Hey, Tenma!

15:19.460 --> 15:23.130
No, no! We're just chatting
while I refuel, that's all!

15:23.213 --> 15:25.132
You can't just spring
something like that on me!

15:25.215 --> 15:27.551
We don't even know each other!
That's impossible!

15:27.635 --> 15:28.636
Right?

15:29.219 --> 15:31.680
It's not like I'm into you or anything.

15:31.764 --> 15:32.723
Sorry.

15:32.806 --> 15:33.849
Huh?

15:33.933 --> 15:36.936
It's not "I wanna go out with her."

15:37.937 --> 15:41.815
It's "I wanna crush you because you're in
my way," so I'm challenging you to a duel.

15:41.899 --> 15:42.816
What?

15:43.776 --> 15:48.155
I think the thing that inspires people
most in this world is sports!

15:48.238 --> 15:50.449
That's why everyone should be watching me!

15:50.532 --> 15:52.910
No, everyone needs to watch me!

15:52.993 --> 15:53.994
Because I'm gonna become

15:54.078 --> 15:58.958
the first true triple-threat athlete
in human history, a Superman!

15:59.041 --> 16:00.834
Triple threat?

16:00.918 --> 16:03.295
You mean like being
both a pitcher and a batter?

16:03.379 --> 16:04.171
Boss!

16:04.254 --> 16:06.966
I looked it up,
and that is not what he means!

16:07.049 --> 16:10.302
- Huh?
- Not a triple threat baseball player!

16:10.386 --> 16:12.221
A triple-threat athlete!

16:12.304 --> 16:13.305
In other words...

16:13.889 --> 16:15.808
Little Senior League baseball!

16:15.891 --> 16:17.726
Ace striker in soccer!

16:17.810 --> 16:19.603
Middle school basketball!

16:19.687 --> 16:23.774
He's the ace in all three, and he keeps
racking up national titles, too!

16:24.608 --> 16:28.278
A Unicorn, the man
with the ultimate physical gift!

16:28.946 --> 16:32.032
MLB, the NBA, the Premier League.

16:32.574 --> 16:35.786
I'm gonna become
the best player in all of them!

16:36.370 --> 16:37.371
What?

16:37.454 --> 16:38.706
Is that even possible?

16:38.789 --> 16:40.040
I have no idea.

16:40.124 --> 16:43.210
I've heard of pros
who can do two sports sometimes, but...

16:43.794 --> 16:45.087
I get it now.

16:45.170 --> 16:47.965
So, basically, you're a sports freak
who loves the spotlight

16:48.048 --> 16:51.218
and can't stand anybody
getting more attention than you.

16:51.301 --> 16:53.846
Huh? "Can't stand"? Not really.

16:54.847 --> 16:57.516
You're just some background extra
from the Home Ec Club, right?

16:57.599 --> 17:00.936
I'm not that interested in people
from some nothing little hobby club

17:01.020 --> 17:02.813
that wouldn't matter
whether it existed or not.

17:03.981 --> 17:04.815
However...

17:04.898 --> 17:06.817
you are annoying.

17:06.900 --> 17:09.486
Hey! What the hell
kind of rude crap is that?

17:09.570 --> 17:12.031
No, I mean,
I'm happy about the rice balls!

17:12.114 --> 17:13.323
It saves me from having to buy food!

17:13.407 --> 17:15.659
- You need to stop talking! Like, now!
- Huh?

17:15.743 --> 17:16.618
It's fine.

17:16.702 --> 17:19.079
Then let's do it. A duel.

17:19.663 --> 17:20.748
Ogami!

17:20.831 --> 17:22.750
He doesn't even sound
like he's dead set on it!

17:22.833 --> 17:25.294
Nope. I'm the one who's pissed off now.

17:25.377 --> 17:29.882
This guy didn't just insult me.
He casually dissed the ladies, too.

17:30.382 --> 17:33.427
I don't care about a Superman hotshot
or your whole triple threat whatever.

17:33.510 --> 17:36.472
Don't look down on Home Ec, dumbass!

17:38.182 --> 17:39.600
All right, it's settled!

17:40.184 --> 17:41.935
What should we compete in?

17:42.478 --> 17:44.188
Okay, let's make it futsal!

17:44.271 --> 17:46.356
One week from now, in the gym.

17:46.857 --> 17:50.110
I'll bring one other person, but you guys
can bring as many as you want.

17:50.194 --> 17:52.905
Huh? Since when do I need a handicap?

17:52.988 --> 17:54.990
No, take the handicap!

17:56.408 --> 18:00.370
Suit yourself, but without one,
this won't even be a match.

18:00.454 --> 18:01.955
Anyway, do what you want.

18:02.581 --> 18:05.250
I'm so sorry, Home Ec Club!

18:05.334 --> 18:07.669
Please let me apologize on his behalf.

18:07.753 --> 18:09.254
Uh, right, okay.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.965
And you all still treat him
like he's special?

18:12.049 --> 18:15.010
Yeah. Normally, if you split your time
between three different sports,

18:15.094 --> 18:16.970
you only have a limited time
for each one, right?

18:17.554 --> 18:22.434
But he overwhelms that limitation
through sheer dominance.

18:22.518 --> 18:25.229
We apologize for how rude he was, too.

18:25.813 --> 18:28.524
But if I may say one thing...

18:29.108 --> 18:33.237
as a teammate he's the greatest hero!

18:33.320 --> 18:35.280
But as an opponent...

18:35.864 --> 18:37.783
he's the strongest villain!

18:39.743 --> 18:41.870
Forget the details.

18:42.454 --> 18:46.875
He looked down on my club members, so
you go out there and wreck his ass, Ogami!

18:46.959 --> 18:49.253
Leave it to me, Boss!

18:49.336 --> 18:51.880
I'll make him regret the day he was born!

18:51.964 --> 18:54.258
This is civilian conversation, right?

18:54.842 --> 18:56.552
But it's futsal, right?

18:56.635 --> 18:58.720
Besides Ogami, who else would even...

18:58.804 --> 19:00.055
Huh? Noren?

19:01.223 --> 19:02.808
You can't just spring
something like that on me!

19:02.891 --> 19:05.644
We don't even know each other!
That's impossible!

19:05.727 --> 19:06.812
Right?

19:06.895 --> 19:09.815
It's not like I'm into you or anything.

19:09.898 --> 19:10.899
Sorry.

19:11.400 --> 19:13.735
This is so humiliating!

19:13.819 --> 19:15.654
I mean, sure,
there was context leading up to it,

19:15.737 --> 19:18.073
but in the end, it totally came off like,
"Stop fighting over me!"

19:18.157 --> 19:21.743
And then, "It's not like I'm into you,"
like I'm some cringey self-important girl!

19:21.827 --> 19:24.580
No, no, overthinking it like that
is way too self-absorbed...

19:24.663 --> 19:26.874
- I won't think about it anymore--
- I'll do it.

19:27.583 --> 19:28.917
Shin?

19:29.001 --> 19:30.586
You were still here?

19:30.669 --> 19:33.213
That guy made my beloved Noren...

19:33.297 --> 19:35.090
"Stop fighting over me!"

19:35.174 --> 19:37.176
"Uh, I'm not into you."

19:37.259 --> 19:39.970
Like she was some cringey
self-important girl! That's unforgivable!

19:40.053 --> 19:43.390
No! Please don't bring it back up again!

19:43.473 --> 19:47.144
Uh, if it doesn't have to be
exactly two-on-two, I could join, too.

19:47.227 --> 19:50.564
The Home Ec Club
isn't just messing around,

19:50.647 --> 19:52.900
and we all take
what we care about seriously.

19:52.983 --> 19:54.109
Kito...

19:54.693 --> 19:56.570
And besides, he made Mitsuoka like...

19:57.154 --> 19:58.947
"Stop fighting over me!"

19:59.031 --> 20:00.616
"Uh, I'm not into you"

20:00.699 --> 20:02.576
like she was
some cringey self-important girl!

20:02.659 --> 20:04.494
Please stop repeating that already!

20:06.079 --> 20:07.331
And anyway...

20:07.414 --> 20:10.918
I don't even care about the whole
"dating as the prize in a duel" thing.

20:11.001 --> 20:12.169
More than anything,

20:12.252 --> 20:16.089
what I can't forgive is him mocking
the Home Ec Club I love so much!

20:16.173 --> 20:17.216
So...

20:17.799 --> 20:20.427
you'd better win, okay?

20:20.510 --> 20:21.637
You got it!

21:56.356 --> 22:00.152
Jeez, asking me out of nowhere to help
with some duel? What the hell is that?

22:00.819 --> 22:04.323
And Mitsuoka... That's the rich girl
at your school, right?

22:04.406 --> 22:05.324
Why her?

22:05.907 --> 22:07.617
Well, no real reason.

22:07.701 --> 22:08.744
Hey!

22:10.454 --> 22:12.289
This is weird.

22:12.372 --> 22:15.250
You've never gone out of your way
to pick a fight with somebody before.

22:15.334 --> 22:18.420
Well, that's because they came
to me first, so it just happened.

22:18.503 --> 22:20.047
Even so!

22:20.130 --> 22:22.716
If you really didn't care at all,
you'd have just ignored them.

22:22.799 --> 22:24.468
Yeah, true.

22:24.551 --> 22:25.635
What is it, though?

22:30.432 --> 22:32.851
When I look at that Ogami guy...

22:32.934 --> 22:35.270
I get all restless. Something about him.

22:38.398 --> 22:41.443
Anyway, I'm only doing
the bare minimum out there.

22:41.526 --> 22:42.944
Yeah, okay!

22:43.028 --> 22:45.363
I wasn't expecting much
from you to begin with.

22:46.823 --> 22:50.285
You always have to add
one extra smart-ass comment!

22:50.869 --> 22:53.622
Crap! I put too much into that
without thinking!

22:55.624 --> 22:56.666
Whoa!

22:57.209 --> 23:01.088
He completely killed that momentum!
He really is nothing short of a prodigy!

23:01.171 --> 23:02.089
Nice pass!

23:02.172 --> 23:04.216
Man, you're irritating!

23:05.467 --> 23:06.510
Another Mitsuoka duel!

23:06.593 --> 23:08.053
And this time, it's against a Unicorn!

23:08.136 --> 23:11.890
- Three-on-two futsal!
- Is this even gonna be a real match?

23:12.474 --> 23:13.600
Listen up.

23:13.683 --> 23:16.686
If you win, then we go
by the usual Mitsuoka duel rules.

23:17.312 --> 23:20.148
But if we win, there's one condition.

23:20.232 --> 23:21.608
What?

23:21.691 --> 23:24.152
You mocked the Home Ec Club.

23:24.236 --> 23:25.862
So, apologize to the ladies.

23:26.446 --> 23:28.073
Huh? Sure, fine.

23:28.615 --> 23:29.783
But are you sure?

23:29.866 --> 23:32.661
That's basically the same thing
as saying, "Don't apologize," you know.

23:32.744 --> 23:34.704
Because I'm absolutely going to win.

23:34.788 --> 23:35.831
What?
